WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.920 --> 00:00:06.210
Welcome everybody

00:00:06.210 --> 00:00:10.083
to the inaugural NIL
Summit and NIL Awards.

00:00:11.940 --> 00:00:14.340
In July, 2022, Atlanta hosted

00:00:14.340 --> 00:00:17.610
what might sound like
a boring legal seminar.

00:00:17.610 --> 00:00:19.020
A conference on the new rules

00:00:19.020 --> 00:00:21.423
around name, image,
and likeness in sports.

00:00:23.730 --> 00:00:25.530
But far from dry and academic,

00:00:25.530 --> 00:00:28.530
the first annual NIL summit was, in fact,

00:00:28.530 --> 00:00:30.960
a flashy star studded event

00:00:30.960 --> 00:00:33.930
put on at the College
Football Hall of Fame.

00:00:33.930 --> 00:00:36.540
And mingling amid the biggest
current and former names

00:00:36.540 --> 00:00:39.690
in sports and media, there
was a crucial cohort,

00:00:39.690 --> 00:00:41.580
the players poised to redefine

00:00:41.580 --> 00:00:44.730
what it means to be a
modern college athlete.

00:00:44.730 --> 00:00:47.940
And the winner of male athlete of the year

00:00:47.940 --> 00:00:50.601
goes to Chase Griffin.

00:00:52.740 --> 00:00:56.550
Among those up and comers,
UCLA's Chase Griffin.

00:00:56.550 --> 00:00:58.410
The UCLA quarterback is among the students

00:00:58.410 --> 00:01:02.250
becoming as well known for
making deals, as making plays.

00:01:02.250 --> 00:01:04.950
And even in that group, Chase stands out.

00:01:04.950 --> 00:01:06.540
My name is Chase Griffin.

00:01:06.540 --> 00:01:07.710
What's up, everyone?

00:01:07.710 --> 00:01:08.880
It's Chase Griffin.

00:01:08.880 --> 00:01:10.830
It's your favorite quarterback's
favorite quarterback,

00:01:10.830 --> 00:01:11.970
Chase Griffin.

00:01:11.970 --> 00:01:15.510
When you look at it as an
empowerment equity opportunity,

00:01:15.510 --> 00:01:19.050
it's really been unmatched
in the sports world

00:01:19.050 --> 00:01:21.840
for any point in time since Title IX.

00:01:21.840 --> 00:01:22.673
Ready, let's go.

00:01:23.730 --> 00:01:24.900
After hardly a full year

00:01:24.900 --> 00:01:27.600
of name, image, and likeness
deals being a reality,

00:01:27.600 --> 00:01:30.642
he already has more than
20 deals with major brands,

00:01:30.642 --> 00:01:33.030
venture and charitable groups,

00:01:33.030 --> 00:01:35.160
all the while balancing
graduating undergrad

00:01:35.160 --> 00:01:37.980
in just two years and
fighting for playing time

00:01:37.980 --> 00:01:38.813
on the field.

00:01:38.813 --> 00:01:40.710
Chase Griffin out of the gun!

00:01:40.710 --> 00:01:42.860
We are joined by UCLA
quarterback, Chase Griffin.

00:01:42.860 --> 00:01:44.730
Not just UCLA quarterback,

00:01:44.730 --> 00:01:46.620
but name, image, likeness superstar.

00:01:46.620 --> 00:01:48.630
I am psyched for this one.

00:01:48.630 --> 00:01:50.250
This kid could actually be the President

00:01:50.250 --> 00:01:52.020
of the United States someday.

00:01:52.020 --> 00:01:54.330
Chase isn't the starting
quarterback for UCLA.

00:01:54.330 --> 00:01:56.460
He's not even the backup quarterback.

00:01:56.460 --> 00:02:00.300
But back on campus in LA, his
nickname is President Chase.

00:02:00.300 --> 00:02:02.490
And after spending a couple
days talking about his approach

00:02:02.490 --> 00:02:04.500
to business, sports, and equality,

00:02:04.500 --> 00:02:05.670
it's not shocking to think

00:02:05.670 --> 00:02:07.770
he might someday hold that office.

00:02:07.770 --> 00:02:11.365
His level of focus and
maturity at this stage,

00:02:11.365 --> 00:02:13.770
I only wish I had.

00:02:13.770 --> 00:02:15.126
If you wanna buy stock in a human being,

00:02:15.126 --> 00:02:16.740
buy stock in Chase Griffin.

00:02:16.740 --> 00:02:18.720
When it comes to building
generational wealth,

00:02:18.720 --> 00:02:21.750
it's not about the money
that you make in college.

00:02:21.750 --> 00:02:24.570
I'm very excited that I
made the amount of money

00:02:24.570 --> 00:02:25.980
that I made last year.

00:02:25.980 --> 00:02:28.380
I am even 10 times more excited

00:02:28.380 --> 00:02:30.423
that I know how to make that money.

00:02:43.080 --> 00:02:44.520
Summer on any college campus

00:02:44.520 --> 00:02:46.830
is mostly for the athletes
who are on lighter,

00:02:46.830 --> 00:02:48.633
but still regimented schedules.

00:02:54.870 --> 00:02:58.170
Attending classes, working out,
a little bit of hanging out,

00:02:58.170 --> 00:03:00.990
and then more working
out on their own time.

00:03:00.990 --> 00:03:02.313
Chase is no exception.

00:03:06.780 --> 00:03:10.590
The 21 year old is a backup,
albeit an impatient one.

00:03:10.590 --> 00:03:12.660
In the topsy-turvy past couple of seasons

00:03:12.660 --> 00:03:15.660
dotted with fanless games
and COVID protocols,

00:03:15.660 --> 00:03:18.210
he's been able to start
three games for the Bruins.

00:03:18.210 --> 00:03:20.400
Griffin with a throw to the end zone!

00:03:20.400 --> 00:03:22.455
Wide open again, touchdown UCLA!

00:03:23.940 --> 00:03:26.100
Beating Arizona, and narrowly losing

00:03:26.100 --> 00:03:28.260
to both Stanford and Oregon.

00:03:28.260 --> 00:03:29.112
That was inches away

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:32.490
from Chase Griffin and UCLA

00:03:32.490 --> 00:03:35.850
being in full fledge comeback mode.

00:03:35.850 --> 00:03:39.030
For Chase, UCLA felt like destiny.

00:03:39.030 --> 00:03:40.890
He was born just a few miles away

00:03:40.890 --> 00:03:44.100
before his family moved to
Texas when he was a toddler.

00:03:44.100 --> 00:03:46.170
But beyond being a sort of homecoming,

00:03:46.170 --> 00:03:50.280
the school's history of athlete
activism was a massive draw.

00:03:50.280 --> 00:03:54.420
I always expected for
myself to have some sort

00:03:54.420 --> 00:03:57.450
of impact that was
beneficial for more people

00:03:57.450 --> 00:04:01.020
than I interact with on a daily basis.

00:04:01.020 --> 00:04:03.273
And in choosing UCLA,

00:04:04.350 --> 00:04:07.650
a lot of that went into me seeing myself

00:04:07.650 --> 00:04:10.860
as someone who reflected the same want

00:04:10.860 --> 00:04:12.420
to make things better

00:04:12.420 --> 00:04:13.800
that so many of the people

00:04:13.800 --> 00:04:16.740
that UCLA prides itself
upon being the home for

00:04:16.740 --> 00:04:17.973
have done in the past.

00:04:26.250 --> 00:04:28.620
The legacies of former UCLA greats,

00:04:28.620 --> 00:04:30.890
like Arthur Ash, Jackie Robinson,

00:04:30.890 --> 00:04:34.230
Kareem Abdul-Jabbar,
and Jackie Joyner-Kersee

00:04:34.230 --> 00:04:36.720
have had a wide ranging impact on society

00:04:36.720 --> 00:04:39.630
well beyond the Westwood campus.

00:04:39.630 --> 00:04:41.670
Chase reveres these people.

00:04:41.670 --> 00:04:44.340
But he's perhaps most
keenly aware of the activism

00:04:44.340 --> 00:04:46.410
of a more recent Bruin alum,

00:04:46.410 --> 00:04:48.870
the basketball player Ed O'Bannon

00:04:48.870 --> 00:04:51.480
Ed O'Bannon, who was the
Naismith Player of the Year,

00:04:51.480 --> 00:04:56.480
national champ, UCLA sports
legend is also a legal hero.

00:04:57.720 --> 00:05:00.270
I think NIL could be the next installment

00:05:00.270 --> 00:05:03.270
where we look back in 30, 40, 50 years,

00:05:03.270 --> 00:05:08.040
and God willing, if we give
him the roses he deserves,

00:05:08.040 --> 00:05:11.362
we add Ed O'Bannon to
that list of UCLA greats.

00:05:13.620 --> 00:05:17.310
O'Bannon, who played at
UCLA from '91 to '95,

00:05:17.310 --> 00:05:19.440
initiated a lawsuit that's widely credited

00:05:19.440 --> 00:05:21.990
for finally opening up the possibility

00:05:21.990 --> 00:05:23.340
of college athletes being paid

00:05:23.340 --> 00:05:25.620
for use of their name,
image, and likeness.

00:05:25.620 --> 00:05:28.560
He sued the NCAA and
video game publisher EA

00:05:28.560 --> 00:05:30.600
for antitrust violations,

00:05:30.600 --> 00:05:32.490
arguing that athletes should be entitled

00:05:32.490 --> 00:05:34.170
to financial compensation

00:05:34.170 --> 00:05:36.423
when schools used their likeness for gain.

00:05:37.380 --> 00:05:40.830
In 2014, a judge ruled in his favor.

00:05:44.818 --> 00:05:46.530
And then on an episode of The Shop,

00:05:46.530 --> 00:05:50.040
surrounded by O' Bannon, Diana
Taurasi, and LeBron James,

00:05:50.040 --> 00:05:51.510
California Governor Gavin Newsom

00:05:51.510 --> 00:05:54.750
signed the first ultimately
successful legislation

00:05:54.750 --> 00:05:57.513
to allow athletes to
receive endorsement deals.

00:05:58.530 --> 00:06:01.500
The Fair Pay to Play Act led
other states to follow suit,

00:06:01.500 --> 00:06:05.130
and ultimately led the
NCAA in 2021 to relent,

00:06:05.130 --> 00:06:06.794
seemingly reluctantly.

00:06:06.794 --> 00:06:11.250
NIL payments were officially
allowed as of July 1st, 2021.

00:06:11.250 --> 00:06:13.710
Today is the last day

00:06:13.710 --> 00:06:15.900
where name, image, and likeness laws

00:06:15.900 --> 00:06:17.280
will not be on the books.

00:06:17.280 --> 00:06:19.530
And kids will not be, if you will,

00:06:19.530 --> 00:06:20.970
not allowed to make money

00:06:20.970 --> 00:06:22.920
off of their name, image, and likeness.

00:06:22.920 --> 00:06:24.360
Making money from jersey sales

00:06:24.360 --> 00:06:26.940
and endorsement deals is
a way for players to share

00:06:26.940 --> 00:06:29.790
in the massively lucrative
world of college athletics.

00:06:29.790 --> 00:06:33.630
This NIL thing is the wild, wild west.

00:06:33.630 --> 00:06:35.790
The NIL change felt like many things

00:06:35.790 --> 00:06:38.910
that happen very slowly, and
then it happened very fast.

00:06:38.910 --> 00:06:42.000
And I wonder for you, having contemplated

00:06:42.000 --> 00:06:44.670
that maybe this was coming at some point,

00:06:44.670 --> 00:06:45.750
how prepared were you?

00:06:45.750 --> 00:06:48.390
What was your mindset
when the switch flipped?

00:06:48.390 --> 00:06:49.260
Right.

00:06:49.260 --> 00:06:50.730
I mean, I still think everyone's

00:06:50.730 --> 00:06:53.040
trying to get prepared for that industry.

00:06:53.040 --> 00:06:55.860
It's still sort of like a wild, wild west.

00:06:55.860 --> 00:06:58.620
I wasn't really expecting anything.

00:06:58.620 --> 00:07:02.670
I was more just thinking about, honestly,

00:07:02.670 --> 00:07:05.877
getting ready for that season, right?

00:07:05.877 --> 00:07:09.693
And capitalizing on
everything that was happening.

00:07:13.260 --> 00:07:16.740
When NIL hit, and it
turned out I had action,

00:07:16.740 --> 00:07:18.180
I was like, oh, okay.

00:07:18.180 --> 00:07:21.150
Well, after this Degree
deal, which was fantastic,

00:07:21.150 --> 00:07:24.000
I was like, okay, I see how I
can be a staple in this game.

00:07:24.000 --> 00:07:26.520
And I see how I can get better over time.

00:07:26.520 --> 00:07:29.530
That's why I teamed up
with my friends at Shell.

00:07:29.530 --> 00:07:31.590
And then the Shell deal hit,
and then Boost Mobile deal hit.

00:07:31.590 --> 00:07:33.090
And then you keep on building, Clearcover.

00:07:33.090 --> 00:07:35.010
Like, you keep on building

00:07:35.010 --> 00:07:37.740
and you get better in the meetings.

00:07:37.740 --> 00:07:41.460
And most of all, you start
seeing where your value

00:07:41.460 --> 00:07:44.193
can be best placed in
these new opportunities.

00:07:46.710 --> 00:07:48.660
The headlines and
storylines and the aftermath

00:07:48.660 --> 00:07:51.660
of the NIL change introduced
visions of instant millionaires

00:07:51.660 --> 00:07:53.613
strolling campuses across the nation.

00:07:54.780 --> 00:07:57.060
You might think the
NIL Athlete of the Year

00:07:57.060 --> 00:07:58.470
lives in splendor,

00:07:58.470 --> 00:08:00.769
or at least in one of
those athletic palaces

00:08:00.769 --> 00:08:04.290
that put most of our
college dorms to shame.

00:08:04.290 --> 00:08:06.513
Well, it's all relative to Chase.

00:08:09.060 --> 00:08:10.170
All right, Jason, so-

00:08:10.170 --> 00:08:11.580
So, here we are, world headquarters.

00:08:11.580 --> 00:08:13.410
Yup, this is where it all happens.

00:08:13.410 --> 00:08:14.910
So this is the kitchen right here.

00:08:14.910 --> 00:08:16.920
Actually, I really enjoy cooking.

00:08:16.920 --> 00:08:17.753
Oh yeah.

00:08:17.753 --> 00:08:20.010
Yeah, this gas oven gets
really hot, really fast.

00:08:20.010 --> 00:08:21.870
So I make pizzas in there.

00:08:21.870 --> 00:08:24.420
This is the best appliance

00:08:24.420 --> 00:08:25.559
since the iPhone, air fryer,

00:08:25.559 --> 00:08:28.080
you can put anything in there.

00:08:28.080 --> 00:08:29.529
I need to do these dishes right here.

00:08:31.110 --> 00:08:33.360
So, no trappings of success yet.

00:08:33.360 --> 00:08:35.520
More a pretty average college dorm room.

00:08:35.520 --> 00:08:36.353
Got my water.

00:08:36.353 --> 00:08:37.530
The fridge filled with leftovers,

00:08:37.530 --> 00:08:40.200
a well used PS4, and of course,

00:08:40.200 --> 00:08:42.660
the requisite Godfather poster.

00:08:42.660 --> 00:08:44.490
It's a far cry from the lifestyle

00:08:44.490 --> 00:08:46.590
seen in some local news reports

00:08:46.590 --> 00:08:49.050
for NIL athletes during this first year.

00:08:49.050 --> 00:08:51.180
Bijan Robinson made headlines

00:08:51.180 --> 00:08:54.453
with an NIL deal with Lamborghini Austin.

00:08:57.330 --> 00:08:59.310
Lamborghinis tend to make more headlines

00:08:59.310 --> 00:09:01.916
than Muhammad Ali or Bruce Lee pictures.

00:09:01.916 --> 00:09:05.040
Some athletes are living in
mansions, driving Lamborghinis.

00:09:05.040 --> 00:09:06.840
As far as I know, you're
doing neither of those things.

00:09:06.840 --> 00:09:08.730
I see where you're living right here.

00:09:08.730 --> 00:09:10.080
It is, with all due respect,

00:09:10.080 --> 00:09:10.913
not a mansion.

00:09:10.913 --> 00:09:12.570
Okay.

00:09:12.570 --> 00:09:14.430
How much of that is a conscious choice?

00:09:14.430 --> 00:09:16.950
And what does it say about
sort of your approach to this?

00:09:16.950 --> 00:09:18.249
Right.

00:09:18.249 --> 00:09:19.530
I mean, first of all, I look at this,

00:09:19.530 --> 00:09:21.540
as like it's my own room,
I got everything I need.

00:09:21.540 --> 00:09:24.000
I'm cool with that, I'm cool
with living below my means.

00:09:24.000 --> 00:09:26.010
I think it's important to remember

00:09:26.010 --> 00:09:30.480
that the volume of financial gain

00:09:30.480 --> 00:09:32.280
is completely overstated.

00:09:32.280 --> 00:09:33.750
And that's sort of y'all's
fault in the media.

00:09:33.750 --> 00:09:34.980
Yeah.
You know, when someone hears

00:09:34.980 --> 00:09:37.770
about a $5 million or a $10 million deal,

00:09:37.770 --> 00:09:39.540
you gotta report it like, oh my goodness.

00:09:39.540 --> 00:09:40.860
people are gonna read this.

00:09:40.860 --> 00:09:42.630
A, I think I'd count two things,

00:09:42.630 --> 00:09:44.950
like how many kids are
even getting these deals?

00:09:44.950 --> 00:09:46.260
Yeah.
And then for the kids

00:09:46.260 --> 00:09:48.570
that do get it, how much
of that is in liquid cash?

00:09:48.570 --> 00:09:50.280
And how much of it is in assets?

00:09:50.280 --> 00:09:52.500
If you pay for a $2 million
house out here in LA

00:09:52.500 --> 00:09:54.330
for a kid to stay in, in
college, that's great.

00:09:54.330 --> 00:09:56.670
But as soon as they're graduated,

00:09:56.670 --> 00:09:57.690
they're not gonna have
the $2 million house.

00:09:57.690 --> 00:09:58.530
They're not, yeah.

00:09:58.530 --> 00:09:59.760
I say the same thing, you know,

00:09:59.760 --> 00:10:02.880
for the kids who who are
driving around in Lamborghinis

00:10:02.880 --> 00:10:04.170
and stuff like that, that's awesome.

00:10:04.170 --> 00:10:05.073
Like, that's super dope.

00:10:05.073 --> 00:10:07.140
And, and I know some of those kids.

00:10:07.140 --> 00:10:10.080
But, you know someone paying
for your lease is different

00:10:10.080 --> 00:10:11.760
than someone actually giving you the value

00:10:11.760 --> 00:10:13.080
of that lease every single month.

00:10:13.080 --> 00:10:16.560
You're investing it,
saving it, 401k, et cetera.

00:10:16.560 --> 00:10:20.516
I say all that, just to
mention that product deals

00:10:20.516 --> 00:10:24.810
and stuff like that are
overhyped by the media.

00:10:24.810 --> 00:10:27.360
And they also can land
kids in some trouble,

00:10:27.360 --> 00:10:29.060
if they're not paying taxes on it.

00:10:31.650 --> 00:10:33.660
That's one of the distinctly unsexy

00:10:33.660 --> 00:10:36.690
and easy to overlook
elements of the new rules.

00:10:36.690 --> 00:10:40.350
Even if an athlete's not getting
cold hard cash from a deal,

00:10:40.350 --> 00:10:42.270
the value of any products given

00:10:42.270 --> 00:10:45.120
are subject to state and federal taxes.

00:10:45.120 --> 00:10:48.000
So, suddenly what a
player sees as free gear

00:10:48.000 --> 00:10:50.640
in return for some social media posts,

00:10:50.640 --> 00:10:53.190
actually equals taxable income.

00:10:53.190 --> 00:10:55.470
And that requires the
same forms you'd fill out

00:10:55.470 --> 00:10:58.470
as an independent
contractor, getting a check.

00:10:58.470 --> 00:11:01.200
I made a fair amount in NIL deals,

00:11:01.200 --> 00:11:03.300
and I invested all of it.

00:11:03.300 --> 00:11:05.160
In my opinion, NIL is great.

00:11:05.160 --> 00:11:06.360
Doing all this is great.

00:11:06.360 --> 00:11:07.620
Making money now is great.

00:11:07.620 --> 00:11:10.590
But the most valuable thing
I've gotten from all of this

00:11:10.590 --> 00:11:13.020
is the fact I'll always
know how to make money

00:11:13.020 --> 00:11:14.760
off of myself.

00:11:14.760 --> 00:11:17.160
All told chase has done more than 20 deals

00:11:17.160 --> 00:11:20.400
with major brands like Degree,
Shell, and Boost Mobile,

00:11:20.400 --> 00:11:21.930
along with venture stage companies

00:11:21.930 --> 00:11:24.870
including Discord, Duffl,
and Creative Juice.

00:11:24.870 --> 00:11:26.760
He's also made a point
to work with charities

00:11:26.760 --> 00:11:28.830
like the Los Angeles Regional Food Bank,

00:11:28.830 --> 00:11:32.163
where he's already raised
funds for almost 60,000 meals.

00:11:36.540 --> 00:11:38.670
This is a song by Javion.

00:11:38.670 --> 00:11:40.103
I heard the opening, I liked it.

00:11:45.090 --> 00:11:48.000
I just took that opening,
and I pitched it slow,

00:11:48.000 --> 00:11:49.293
or I think I sped it.

00:11:52.470 --> 00:11:54.780
At his desk, when he's not making music,

00:11:54.780 --> 00:11:56.340
another side project,

00:11:56.340 --> 00:11:59.430
he's either networking with
CEOs or investors he seeks out,

00:11:59.430 --> 00:12:03.003
or who seek him out, or
negotiating new deals.

00:12:03.840 --> 00:12:05.070
Hey Mallory

00:12:05.070 --> 00:12:06.270
Hi Chase, how are you doing?

00:12:06.270 --> 00:12:07.103
I'm doing well.

00:12:07.103 --> 00:12:08.820
I'm turning on my camera right now.

00:12:08.820 --> 00:12:10.023
Yeah, no worries.

00:12:12.540 --> 00:12:14.790
This is an average NIL deal.

00:12:14.790 --> 00:12:16.350
A brand approaches an athlete

00:12:16.350 --> 00:12:18.630
who can help spread their
message to a demographic

00:12:18.630 --> 00:12:21.540
they believe the athlete can help reach.

00:12:21.540 --> 00:12:24.030
In this case, DirectTV
is looking to market

00:12:24.030 --> 00:12:26.910
their NFL Sunday Ticket
to college students.

00:12:26.910 --> 00:12:29.910
There'd be two posts,
one post late August,

00:12:29.910 --> 00:12:32.550
and one post on the
first week of September.

00:12:32.550 --> 00:12:35.817
And the compensation
would be 1200 per post.

00:12:35.817 --> 00:12:36.650
Okay.

00:12:36.650 --> 00:12:37.860
So it'd be 2400 total.

00:12:37.860 --> 00:12:40.320
Right, perfect, are they video posts

00:12:40.320 --> 00:12:43.110
or are they, you know, pic and caption?

00:12:43.110 --> 00:12:44.070
They can be either.

00:12:44.070 --> 00:12:46.020
It's up to you guys.

00:12:46.020 --> 00:12:47.880
So that was pretty good.

00:12:47.880 --> 00:12:51.060
400 above what they had originally asked.

00:12:51.060 --> 00:12:54.060
So, that's a win.

00:12:54.060 --> 00:12:55.650
So, yeah, I mean, at this point

00:12:55.650 --> 00:12:58.980
after I do a zoom or something like that,

00:12:58.980 --> 00:13:00.810
I either chill out, go back to laying down

00:13:00.810 --> 00:13:02.850
if I was watching a movie or something,

00:13:02.850 --> 00:13:05.250
or, you know, go to YouTube

00:13:05.250 --> 00:13:07.803
to start looking for more samples.

00:13:10.809 --> 00:13:13.680
♪ This is presidential, Chase ♪

00:13:13.680 --> 00:13:15.090
It's a pretty simple interaction

00:13:15.090 --> 00:13:17.760
for Chase and for DirectTV.

00:13:17.760 --> 00:13:20.640
Negotiated over a couple
of emails and zoom calls

00:13:20.640 --> 00:13:21.930
and papered with a contract

00:13:21.930 --> 00:13:24.690
Chase will have his dad
look over before he signs.

00:13:24.690 --> 00:13:26.220
And Chase, who's made himself

00:13:26.220 --> 00:13:29.490
as much of a student of
the new NIL marketplace

00:13:29.490 --> 00:13:32.490
as he has of public policy at UCLA,

00:13:32.490 --> 00:13:35.040
says he understands why it's working.

00:13:35.040 --> 00:13:37.830
A brand ambassadorship with an athlete

00:13:37.830 --> 00:13:40.350
is more attractive to these brands now,

00:13:40.350 --> 00:13:41.730
as far as return on investment

00:13:41.730 --> 00:13:45.599
than even a a post by a famous actor.

00:13:48.900 --> 00:13:50.100
If there's any place to learn

00:13:50.100 --> 00:13:52.530
that sports are deep in
the hearts of Americans,

00:13:52.530 --> 00:13:55.113
it's on a high school
football field in Texas.

00:14:01.560 --> 00:14:03.390
Friday night lights in the Lone Star State

00:14:03.390 --> 00:14:04.950
might be the gridiron equivalent

00:14:04.950 --> 00:14:07.020
of Frank Sinatra's New York City.

00:14:07.020 --> 00:14:09.870
Making it there means
you're something special.

00:14:09.870 --> 00:14:13.980
Chase Griffin, quarterback,
class of '19, Hutto, Texas.

00:14:13.980 --> 00:14:16.500
And Chase didn't just
make it, he excelled.

00:14:16.500 --> 00:14:19.110
Let's talk about some
of the top quarterbacks

00:14:19.110 --> 00:14:19.943
in the state.

00:14:19.943 --> 00:14:22.020
And when you look at that
list, at the top of it,

00:14:22.020 --> 00:14:23.876
you gotta talk about Chase Griffin.

00:14:23.876 --> 00:14:26.490
I was lucky to play three
years as a quarterback

00:14:26.490 --> 00:14:29.820
for Hutto High School,
which is a one horse town.

00:14:29.820 --> 00:14:31.680
We've had great success.

00:14:31.680 --> 00:14:33.420
And so the town really shut down

00:14:33.420 --> 00:14:35.118
and came out and supported
us every Friday night.

00:14:36.060 --> 00:14:36.893
Chase right, straight back.
There's CJ right there.

00:14:36.893 --> 00:14:39.270
And he's wide open, if he can catch it.

00:14:39.270 --> 00:14:41.253
Nice!
He does, touchdown Hippos!

00:14:42.180 --> 00:14:46.230
Chase one word to describe
that finish to that game.

00:14:46.230 --> 00:14:47.583
God, that's it.

00:14:48.450 --> 00:14:49.950
Coming from a town like that,

00:14:49.950 --> 00:14:53.850
where football was so prioritized,
it has its pros and cons.

00:14:53.850 --> 00:14:54.990
But I think on the pro side,

00:14:54.990 --> 00:14:57.480
I learned how to win, how to get better.

00:14:57.480 --> 00:14:59.280
And most importantly what it's like

00:14:59.280 --> 00:15:01.953
to build a team where
everyone gets better.

00:15:11.850 --> 00:15:13.590
Emulating his UCLA alumni

00:15:13.590 --> 00:15:16.740
like Robinson, Joyner-Kersee,
and Abdul-Jabbar,

00:15:16.740 --> 00:15:19.080
Chase is looking at the
impact NIL will have,

00:15:19.080 --> 00:15:22.410
not just for him, but the
athletes that will follow.

00:15:22.410 --> 00:15:24.840
When the predecessors
who have come before you

00:15:24.840 --> 00:15:25.860
have changed the world

00:15:25.860 --> 00:15:28.710
and made life better for everyone today,

00:15:28.710 --> 00:15:32.040
you can't help but ask
yourself how the actions

00:15:32.040 --> 00:15:34.740
that you're taking now, and
the companies and brands

00:15:34.740 --> 00:15:36.750
in the NIL space that you work with,

00:15:36.750 --> 00:15:41.670
are all cumulative, really
building something greater

00:15:41.670 --> 00:15:43.383
than any of us could foresee.

00:15:49.530 --> 00:15:51.360
I've actually, I've never moderated.

00:15:51.360 --> 00:15:52.830
So this will be my first time.

00:15:52.830 --> 00:15:53.793
It should be fun.

00:15:54.720 --> 00:15:56.403
I know my handwriting's terrible.

00:15:58.020 --> 00:15:59.070
The last day of the conference,

00:15:59.070 --> 00:16:00.840
Chase was asked to co-moderate a panel

00:16:00.840 --> 00:16:04.083
with Monique Nelson, the
CEO for UniWorld group.

00:16:04.083 --> 00:16:07.410
All right, I'm excited to be here.

00:16:07.410 --> 00:16:09.690
UniWorld group is one
of the longest-standing

00:16:09.690 --> 00:16:12.360
multicultural advertising
and marketing agencies

00:16:12.360 --> 00:16:13.890
in the United States.

00:16:13.890 --> 00:16:14.970
The firm works with brands

00:16:14.970 --> 00:16:17.370
like Ford, Home Depot,
and Johnson &amp; Johnson

00:16:17.370 --> 00:16:19.980
to help reach the black
and brown communities.

00:16:19.980 --> 00:16:22.530
And they have big ambitions in NIL.

00:16:22.530 --> 00:16:27.530
For UniWorld group, the
idea of this was pretty epic

00:16:27.690 --> 00:16:31.080
in that because we serve the undervalued,

00:16:31.080 --> 00:16:34.320
overlooked, and the underserved,

00:16:34.320 --> 00:16:36.630
we knew that this
particular group of people

00:16:36.630 --> 00:16:39.025
would fall into that category.

00:16:39.025 --> 00:16:44.025
And we plan on being the premier
practice for NIL athletes

00:16:45.630 --> 00:16:50.630
that are looking to do
purpose-driven media advertising

00:16:50.970 --> 00:16:53.463
community-level engagement work.

00:16:54.690 --> 00:16:57.630
UWG launched a program called the NILE

00:16:57.630 --> 00:17:01.080
to help black student athletes
partner with major brands.

00:17:01.080 --> 00:17:03.540
But to help them
understand how to do that,

00:17:03.540 --> 00:17:05.130
they brought on Chase to serve

00:17:05.130 --> 00:17:08.670
as a student athlete
executive in residence.

00:17:08.670 --> 00:17:11.520
For me, I do nothing
without tremendous amounts

00:17:11.520 --> 00:17:13.950
of data for all of our clients.

00:17:13.950 --> 00:17:17.040
I really wanted to be
thoughtful about this practice

00:17:17.040 --> 00:17:19.500
being very athlete-centric.

00:17:19.500 --> 00:17:21.840
If I were to build it or anyone
on my team were to build it,

00:17:21.840 --> 00:17:26.010
it would not have the athlete at the core.

00:17:26.010 --> 00:17:29.280
When, you know, you're 18, 19, 20, 21, 22,

00:17:29.280 --> 00:17:33.270
the best way to have
credibility is confidence.

00:17:33.270 --> 00:17:36.390
And the only way for
confidence, to be authentic.

00:17:36.390 --> 00:17:38.430
I'm actually learning on the job.

00:17:38.430 --> 00:17:41.760
I'm learning about the brand side of NIL,

00:17:41.760 --> 00:17:43.620
but I'm also trying to make sure

00:17:43.620 --> 00:17:46.200
that empowerment equity is built in,

00:17:46.200 --> 00:17:50.163
especially for black student
athletes in the NIL world.

00:17:50.163 --> 00:17:53.280
ROI, return on investment.

00:17:53.280 --> 00:17:54.113
Athletes

00:17:54.113 --> 00:17:56.280
Both Chase and UWG see NIL deals

00:17:56.280 --> 00:17:59.103
as something much more than
making money for students.

00:18:02.790 --> 00:18:04.860
It's also a potential investment

00:18:04.860 --> 00:18:06.750
in a community long overlooked.

00:18:06.750 --> 00:18:09.780
I think we're getting
ready to stock boxes,

00:18:09.780 --> 00:18:11.380
trying to feed the people of LA.

00:18:12.420 --> 00:18:14.610
A piece of each of Chase's NIL deals

00:18:14.610 --> 00:18:17.040
go to his BE11EVE BRAND campaign,

00:18:17.040 --> 00:18:19.860
which has raised more
than $13,000 for meals

00:18:19.860 --> 00:18:22.950
for the LA Food Bank backpack program.

00:18:22.950 --> 00:18:25.860
But athletes giving back is only one side.

00:18:25.860 --> 00:18:27.960
I'm here with LegalZoom
to give you five tips

00:18:27.960 --> 00:18:29.880
on the NIL game plan.

00:18:29.880 --> 00:18:31.140
UWG and Chase believe

00:18:31.140 --> 00:18:33.330
having brands investing in the athletes,

00:18:33.330 --> 00:18:36.840
especially athletes of color,
can be a force multiplier

00:18:36.840 --> 00:18:39.780
for these historically
marginalized communities.

00:18:39.780 --> 00:18:42.420
When you look at the
revenue-generating sports,

00:18:42.420 --> 00:18:45.900
football and basketball, 88%
of those athletes are black.

00:18:45.900 --> 00:18:47.760
So when you're doing stuff

00:18:47.760 --> 00:18:50.370
to empower student
athletes in the NIL space,

00:18:50.370 --> 00:18:53.130
you're also helping to
deliver on your promise.

00:18:53.130 --> 00:18:54.750
Now, student athletes
are not the only ones

00:18:54.750 --> 00:18:57.180
who should receive this
help, by any means.

00:18:57.180 --> 00:18:59.040
But statistically, by doing that,

00:18:59.040 --> 00:19:00.630
you're gonna be delivering
on your mission.

00:19:00.630 --> 00:19:03.660
Additionally, student
athletes, on average,

00:19:03.660 --> 00:19:06.360
come from lower levels of income.

00:19:06.360 --> 00:19:09.000
So, you're also delivering
on that promise.

00:19:09.000 --> 00:19:12.240
And a lot of these student
athletes are first generation.

00:19:12.240 --> 00:19:14.070
They're first gen college students.

00:19:14.070 --> 00:19:16.380
Some of them first gen
high school diploma.

00:19:16.380 --> 00:19:19.080
Some of them first time
receiving the amount of money

00:19:19.080 --> 00:19:22.593
that they received in their families.

00:19:26.730 --> 00:19:30.443
This has been a wild first year in NIL.

00:19:30.443 --> 00:19:32.250
We all knew that there would
be bags of cash around, right?

00:19:32.250 --> 00:19:33.690
There's always been bags of cash.

00:19:33.690 --> 00:19:35.490
There's cash everywhere.

00:19:35.490 --> 00:19:38.100
What we know is that
that's not sustainable.

00:19:38.100 --> 00:19:42.390
We know that athletics has
an expiration date on it.

00:19:42.390 --> 00:19:44.670
So for us, inclusion ultimately means

00:19:44.670 --> 00:19:46.650
this is just a part of you.

00:19:46.650 --> 00:19:48.000
It is a tremendous part of you,

00:19:48.000 --> 00:19:50.130
and we are gonna celebrate
that part of you.

00:19:50.130 --> 00:19:52.440
But we also know that
you're bigger than that.

00:19:52.440 --> 00:19:56.550
So we wanna empower you to
live past your expiration date

00:19:56.550 --> 00:19:58.440
for this part of your life.

00:19:58.440 --> 00:20:01.200
And quite honestly have
equity in everything

00:20:01.200 --> 00:20:05.253
that you have poured yourself
into as an NIL athlete.

00:20:11.040 --> 00:20:12.660
It may still be the wild west days

00:20:12.660 --> 00:20:14.430
for the NIL industry,

00:20:14.430 --> 00:20:17.280
but in the first year,
about a billion dollars

00:20:17.280 --> 00:20:20.610
in business was done with NCAA athletes.

00:20:20.610 --> 00:20:23.670
For the early leaders in
the NIL space like Chase,

00:20:23.670 --> 00:20:26.850
they're striking a precedent
for athletes that follow them.

00:20:26.850 --> 00:20:29.100
And that's important,
because collegiate athletes

00:20:29.100 --> 00:20:31.770
don't have that much time to profit.

00:20:31.770 --> 00:20:36.540
Only an estimated 2% of NCAA
athletes go on to the pros.

00:20:36.540 --> 00:20:38.640
Even the hardest working are often limited

00:20:38.640 --> 00:20:40.830
by things they can't control.

00:20:40.830 --> 00:20:43.083
For chase, it's been his height.

00:20:48.810 --> 00:20:50.220
I'm 5'10" now.

00:20:50.220 --> 00:20:52.530
In high school, after my sophomore year,

00:20:52.530 --> 00:20:57.060
when I threw for 3000 yards, I
was probably like 5'6', 5'5".

00:20:57.060 --> 00:20:58.620
I mean, I could arguably say

00:20:58.620 --> 00:21:00.660
I'm one of the best in the history

00:21:00.660 --> 00:21:03.180
of Texas high school
football, but you know,

00:21:03.180 --> 00:21:04.770
I've gone through the height test

00:21:04.770 --> 00:21:06.600
where they'll call you outta class,

00:21:06.600 --> 00:21:08.790
shake your hand, look at you up and down,

00:21:08.790 --> 00:21:11.820
and be like, "Nice to meet
you, you go back to class."

00:21:11.820 --> 00:21:13.530
It's a sad, but timeless story

00:21:13.530 --> 00:21:15.090
for student athletes.

00:21:15.090 --> 00:21:17.010
And for Chase, his story is something

00:21:17.010 --> 00:21:18.570
he's not shied away from,

00:21:18.570 --> 00:21:21.600
but embraced when it
comes to his NIL deals.

00:21:21.600 --> 00:21:24.120
I'm frequently the smallest
person on the football field,

00:21:24.120 --> 00:21:26.068
but I always strive to
be the most impactful.

00:21:27.570 --> 00:21:29.763
My middle school coach told me

00:21:29.763 --> 00:21:32.283
that I would never play in high school.

00:21:33.210 --> 00:21:35.460
Chase's deals with Degree's
Breaking Limits Team

00:21:35.460 --> 00:21:37.800
and Clearcover's Inspired Underdogs

00:21:37.800 --> 00:21:40.470
allowed him to capitalize
financially from football,

00:21:40.470 --> 00:21:44.100
even though last season, he
never saw the field for UCLA.

00:21:44.100 --> 00:21:45.810
I play football because I love the game.

00:21:45.810 --> 00:21:48.150
I play the football because
I'm a good competitor.

00:21:48.150 --> 00:21:49.380
I love to compete.

00:21:49.380 --> 00:21:51.397
And I play football
because I'm good at it.

00:21:51.397 --> 00:21:52.410
At the end of the day,

00:21:52.410 --> 00:21:54.720
I don't play football for my livelihood,

00:21:54.720 --> 00:21:56.040
which is important to remember

00:21:56.040 --> 00:21:58.560
when it comes down to identity.

00:21:58.560 --> 00:21:59.730
I'm myself, Chase Griffin.

00:21:59.730 --> 00:22:02.703
As long as I'm that, I got
something in this world.

00:22:09.030 --> 00:22:10.470
As he moves into the new season

00:22:10.470 --> 00:22:13.050
and focuses more on
football than business,

00:22:13.050 --> 00:22:14.652
Chase doesn't see much
of a differentiation

00:22:14.652 --> 00:22:17.790
between the two in terms of his mindset.

00:22:17.790 --> 00:22:21.840
I wouldn't be surprised if
I wasn't playing football

00:22:21.840 --> 00:22:25.080
in five years and was
running fortune 500 company.

00:22:25.080 --> 00:22:26.430
But I also wouldn't be surprised

00:22:26.430 --> 00:22:29.520
if I was winning the Super
Bowl 5, 10 years from now.

00:22:29.520 --> 00:22:32.604
And either way, I'm gonna
keep on working at the tools

00:22:32.604 --> 00:22:37.193
that would align myself
and my future with both.

00:22:37.193 --> 00:22:38.910
And at the end of the day,

00:22:38.910 --> 00:22:40.890
you're always gonna have yourself.

00:22:40.890 --> 00:22:42.600
If you can make profit off of yourself,

00:22:42.600 --> 00:22:46.140
and know where you add value
in any world you're in,

00:22:46.140 --> 00:22:47.190
you'll be able to adapt

00:22:47.190 --> 00:22:49.743
and find ways to generate
wealth for yourself.

